=== Welcome to Collider.JAM {{ .releaseName }}!

_Version: {{ .version }}_

_Collider.JAM_ is a delightful JavaScript game framework hand-crafted for game jamming, prototyping, creative coding, indie game development, and beyond. It is tuned for nimble development with minimal noise.

It conceals rough _JavaScript_ edges and heavy APIs,
turning development into a joyride.
_JavaScript_ is a pleasant language when you don't have to deal with _HTML_, _DOM_, _CSS_, and _nonsense frameworks_.


_Collider.JAM_ follows the web-first development model, but the code is portable across many platforms - web, desktops (_Linux_, _macOS_, and _Windows_), and mobile (_Android_ and _iOS_).

_Collider.JAM_ is a perfect tool to unlock your creativity and deliver the next great game.

Check out [the installation instructions](#.install).
The best way to install is to run:

    npm i -g collider.jam

[Getting Started](#.getting-started) guides you on how to setup a new project and have something moving on the screen.

The design philosophy of the framework is explored in [the Design section](#.design).


Other sections worth checking:

* [the root node](#./) - covers the scene graph structure
* [tips](#.tips)

